stream->avail_out = len;
```

`stream->avail_out` is of type `uInt` which is typically `unsigned int` (32-bit). If `len` (which is `size_t`, 64-bit on 64-bit systems) is larger than `UINT_MAX`, it gets truncated. But `len` is `scanline_width` which is at most a few MB, so this shouldn't be an issue.

