static int read_scanline_bytes(spng_ctx *ctx, z_stream *stream, unsigned char *dest, size_t len)
{
    ...
    stream->avail_out = len;
    stream->next_out = dest;

    if(!stream->avail_in)
    {
        ret = read_idat_bytes(ctx, &bytes_read);
        ...
    }

    do
    {
        ret = inflate(stream, Z_SYNC_FLUSH);
        ...
    }while(stream->avail_out != 0);
    ...
}
```

If `len` is 0, then `stream->avail_out` is 0, and the do-while loop runs once with `avail_out = 0`. `inflate` with `avail_out = 0` returns `Z_BUF_ERROR` or `Z_OK`. If it returns `Z_OK`, the loop condition `stream->avail_out != 0` is false, so it exits. This seems fine.

